    about: {
      title: 'Association history',
      heroText:
        "I am Corinne Rodier, President of the Wink Monaco association, but also the *mother* of Thomas, visually impaired since a young age.\n\nIn January 2023, with several of his former classmates, we decided to create this association, so that history does not repeat itself...\n\nHere is his journey:\nFrom a young age, Thomas complained about his « poor vision » (he missed steps in the stairs, bumped into things...). Certain alarming signs led him to a series of medical appointments, orthoptists, occupational therapists... Without ever finding a concrete answer to what was happening to him.\n\nIt was only at the age of 19, after years of *frustration* and *misunderstanding*, that Thomas was finally able to *articulate* or give a *name* to his struggles and finally understood why he was different. It was after a *simple* « visual field » examination that the diagnosis was made: he suffers from « retinitis pigmentosa », a degenerative disease of the retina that affects both eyes and will eventually make him completely blind over time.\n\nBetter knowledge would have allowed him to *understand* his handicap in daily life, better care could have perhaps enabled him to gain precious years of sight (including better eye protection, special lenses, appropriate vitamin intake...).\n\nUnfortunately, Thomas's experience is not an isolated case; many people, young or less young, also suffer from diseases that cause loss of hearing or sight and realize it too late, unfortunately, far too late...",
    },
